        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: কোটা",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "কোটা — koṭā — \"to chop (vegetables or fish)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "আমি রাতের জন্য সবজি কুটলাম। Āmi rāter jônyô sôbji kuṭlām. I chopped vegetables for dinner."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he/she …): তিনি মাছ কুটলেন, tini māchh kuṭlen."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The stem vowel rises in the past: কুটলাম, I chopped."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "কোটা (koṭā) is a tadbhava: CDIAL lists Bengali kuṭā, \"to cut up for cooking\", and koṭā under Sanskrit kuṭṭayati, \"crushes, pounds\" (CDIAL 3241)."
            }
          ]
        },
